    "updated_at": "2023-06-15T07:35:36Z",
    "body": "Since the publicized name in blogs etc. has been [origin private file system](https://www.google.com/search?q=%22origin+private+file+system%22), I wonder what we do \"brand\"-wise. Would it be fair to keep saying \"origin private file system\" in general, and then more concretely say that \"the  _origin private file system_ can contain one or multiple _bucket file systems_\"? ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
